    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d133-a1">

                <pb facs="0325" n="315" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg315"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure 1 in No. 2]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Gardner to Mr. Hamilton.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Custom-House,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-02-27"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 27, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> With reference to your letter of the 25th
                    instant, I am desired to transmit to you herewith, for the information of the
                    lords commissioners of her Majesty’s treasury, copy of a report, with its
                    enclosure, which the board have received from their collector at Liverpool with
                    respect to a statement alleged to have been made by him concerning the shipment
                    of guns in the Gibraltar, and referred to in page 8 of the Parliamentary Return,
                    date 20th July, 1863, No. 461.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>F. G. GARDNER.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
